      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/troy_hills_new_jersey",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Troy Hills Historic District, with 15 homes dating from 1720 to 1920, was added to the New Jersey Register of Historic Places in 2015.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/troy_hills_new_jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "European settlers first arrived in the area around 1715, establishing Troy Village by 1720 along Troy Brook.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/troy_hills_new_jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The township that now contains Troy Hills was incorporated in 1928 from parts of Hanover Township, shifting from farms to suburban neighborhoods after WWII.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/troy_hills_new_jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Archaeological digs at the Dale Road rockshelter reveal summer camps from 6,000 years ago, showing the Lenni‑Lenape used the area for hunting and fishing.",
